DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     ccoommpprreessss exits 0 on success; 1 if a named file is not a
     regular file, has other links, or if an argument or input
     file is malformed (missing option argument, bad magic num-
     ber, or a code width the binary cannot handle); and 2 if
     compressing a file did not save space and -ff was not given,
     in which case the input file is left unchanged and no .ZZ
     file is kept.

NNOOTTEESS
     An interrupt or an unexpected fault while decompressing
     removes the partially written output file rather than
     leaving a truncated one behind.
